#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Behavioral Biases in Trading]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Psychological factors influencing decisions 🧠]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Can lead to suboptimal choices 📉]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Behavioral biases are psychological factors that influence trading decisions. They can cause traders to deviate from rational, optimal strategies.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("These biases can lead to suboptimal choices, negatively impacting trading performance.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Overconfidence Bias]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Overestimating one's abilities 💪]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Leads to excessive trading, risk-taking 🎲]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Example: Frequent trading despite losses 📈📉]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("One common bias is overconfidence, where traders overestimate their abilities and knowledge.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("This can lead to excessive trading and risk-taking, as traders believe they can consistently beat the market.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("For example, an overconfident trader might continue to trade frequently despite a string of losses, convinced that their strategy will eventually pay off.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Loss Aversion Bias]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Avoiding losses over seeking gains 😰]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Holding losing positions too long 📉🕰️]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Example: Not selling a losing stock 📉🙅]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Another bias is loss aversion, where traders feel the pain of losses more intensely than the pleasure of gains.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("This can cause traders to hold onto losing positions for too long, hoping they'll recover their losses.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("For instance, a loss-averse trader might refuse to sell a losing stock, even as it continues to decline in value.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Impact on Trading Strategies]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Deviating from optimal strategies 📊❌]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Increased risk, reduced profitability 📈📉💸]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Behavioral biases can cause traders to deviate from optimal trading strategies that would maximize their returns while minimizing risk.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("As a result, biased trading decisions can lead to increased risk exposure and reduced profitability over time.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Mitigating Behavioral Biases]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Awareness of biases 🧠✅]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Sticking to a trading plan 📝📈]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Seeking objective feedback 🗣️🤝]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("To mitigate the impact of behavioral biases, traders should first become aware of their existence and potential influence.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("Developing and adhering to a well-defined trading plan can help traders stay disciplined and avoid emotional decision-making.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("Finally, seeking objective feedback from peers or mentors can provide a reality check and help traders identify when biases may be affecting their judgment.")
]
]